{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4789-a012-3456789abcde",
    "name": "NEOCOM Back",
    "description": "Unique neocom-back collection for every HTTP endpoint currently served by the Nest app, aligned with OpenAPI under tools/openapi/ and ExceptionCatalog outcomes.\n\n**Specs covered**\n- `pilot-service-v0.1.0.yaml` \u2014 GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}\n- `industry-service-v0.1.0.yaml` \u2014 GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}/blueprints\n- Auth \u2014 POST /v1/auth/callback + GET /v1/auth/session (Postman bootstrap) + TOKEN_UNAVAILABLE via access-cookie middleware\n\n**Authentication (outside Postman)**\n1. Log in with **neocom-front** against this back (SSO \u2192 `POST /v1/auth/callback` \u2192 `tokens.json`).\n2. In Postman, run **Session \u2192 00 Load session from back** to fill `neocomAccessCookie`, `characterId`, `pilotId`.\n3. Authenticated requests send `Cookie: neocom_access={{neocomAccessCookie}}`.\n\nUse the **NEOCOM local** environment.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "pilotId",
      "value": "93813310"
    },
    {
      "key": "unknownPilotId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "invalidPilotId",
      "value": "not-a-number"
    },
    {
      "key": "authorization",
      "value": "present"
    },
    {
      "key": "authCode",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "authState",
      "value": "test-state"
    },
    {
      "key": "ssoStateCookie",
      "value": "test-state"
    },
    {
      "key": "mismatchedAuthState",
      "value": "wrong-state"
    },
    {
      "key": "invalidAccessCookie",
      "value": "expired|Pilot|1"
    },
    {
      "key": "neocomAccessCookie",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "characterId",
      "value": "92002067"
    },
    {
      "key": "characterName",
      "value": "Adam Antinoo"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level helpers are inlined per request for Postman/Newman compatibility."
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Session \u2014 load auth from back",
      "description": "Authenticate **outside** Postman (neocom-front SSO). The back stores tokens in `tokens.json`.\n\nRun **00** once to pull `neocom_access` (+ character fields) into the NEOCOM local environment. Then use Pilot / Industry authenticated requests.",
      "auth": {
        "type": "noauth"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "00 Load session from back",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/session?characterId={{characterId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "session"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "characterId",
                  "value": "{{characterId}}",
                  "description": "Optional. Empty = first character in tokens.json"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a prior front login so `tokens.json` has the character. Returns JSON for Postman env vars and sets `Set-Cookie: neocom_access=\u2026`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.environment.name) {",
                  "  console.warn('Select the NEOCOM local environment so neocomAccessCookie persists.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('session payload', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.characterId).to.be.a('number');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.characterName).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.neocomAccessCookie).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.cookieName).to.eql('neocom_access');",
                  "});",
                  "function write(key, value) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(key, value);",
                  "  try { pm.environment.set(key, value); } catch (e) {}",
                  "}",
                  "write('neocomAccessCookie', body.neocomAccessCookie);",
                  "write('characterId', String(body.characterId));",
                  "write('characterName', body.characterName);",
                  "write('pilotId', String(body.pilotId || body.characterId));",
                  "write('authorization', body.authorization || 'present');",
                  "console.log('Session bound as', body.characterName, body.characterId);",
                  "if (Array.isArray(body.characters)) {",
                  "  console.log('Stored characters:', body.characters.map(c => c.characterId + ':' + c.characterName).join(', '));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "00b Load session (first stored character)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/session",
            "description": "Same as 00 without characterId \u2014 binds the first entry in tokens.json."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('session payload', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.characterId).to.be.a('number');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.characterName).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.neocomAccessCookie).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.cookieName).to.eql('neocom_access');",
                  "});",
                  "function write(key, value) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(key, value);",
                  "  try { pm.environment.set(key, value); } catch (e) {}",
                  "}",
                  "write('neocomAccessCookie', body.neocomAccessCookie);",
                  "write('characterId', String(body.characterId));",
                  "write('characterName', body.characterName);",
                  "write('pilotId', String(body.pilotId || body.characterId));",
                  "write('authorization', body.authorization || 'present');",
                  "console.log('Session bound as', body.characterName, body.characterId);",
                  "if (Array.isArray(body.characters)) {",
                  "  console.log('Stored characters:', body.characters.map(c => c.characterId + ':' + c.characterName).join(', '));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pilot \u2014 GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}",
      "description": "OpenAPI: tools/openapi/pilot-service-v0.1.0.yaml\nOutcomes: 200 PublicPilotV1 | 200 PilotV2 | 400 INVALID_REQUEST | 404 NOT_FOUND | 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR (PILOT_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "200 \u2014 PublicPilotV1 (anonymous)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}",
            "description": "No Authorization header. Expect PublicPilotV1; private PilotV2 fields omitted."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('jsonClass is PublicPilotV1', () => pm.expect(body.jsonClass).to.eql('PublicPilotV1'));",
                  "pm.test('returns requested pilotId', () => pm.expect(body.pilotId).to.eql(Number(pm.variables.get('pilotId'))));",
                  "pm.test('omits private PilotV2 fields', () => {",
                  "  ['totalSkillpoints','walletBalance','currentShipName','currentShipTypeName','lastKnownLocation'].forEach((k) => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(k);",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "200 \u2014 PilotV2 (logged in)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "{{authorization}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}",
            "description": "Any non-empty Authorization marks the caller logged in (value is not validated as a token). Expect PilotV2 when the source has private fields."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('jsonClass is PilotV2', () => pm.expect(body.jsonClass).to.eql('PilotV2'));",
                  "pm.test('returns requested pilotId', () => pm.expect(body.pilotId).to.eql(Number(pm.variables.get('pilotId'))));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "400 \u2014 INVALID_REQUEST (pilotId not integer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{invalidPilotId}}",
            "description": "ExceptionCatalog.INVALID_PILOT_ID \u2192 HTTP 400, code INVALID_REQUEST."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('NeocomError INVALID_REQUEST on pilotId', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].code).to.eql('INVALID_REQUEST');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].description).to.eql('pilotId must be an integer.');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].field).to.eql('pilotId');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].container).to.eql('path');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].value).to.eql(pm.variables.get('invalidPilotId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "404 \u2014 NOT_FOUND (unknown pilot)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{unknownPilotId}}",
            "description": "ExceptionCatalog.NOT_FOUND when ESI returns not-found for the character. Use a pilotId ESI does not know (default unknownPilotId=1)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('NeocomError NOT_FOUND', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].code).to.eql('NOT_FOUND');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].field).to.eql('pilotId');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].container).to.eql('path');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].value).to.eql(String(pm.variables.get('unknownPilotId')));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "500 \u2014 PILOT_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}",
            "description": "ExceptionCatalog.PILOT_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE when ESI is network/server-error. Only returns 500 when the pilot source fails \u2014 leave disabled in happy-path runs, or break ESI connectivity to exercise."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 500 when source unavailable', () => pm.response.to.have.status(500));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('NeocomError INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].code).to.eql('INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].description).to.eql('The pilot source is not available.');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Industry \u2014 GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}/blueprints",
      "description": "OpenAPI: tools/openapi/industry-service-v0.1.0.yaml\nOutcomes: 200 BlueprintV1[] | 400 INVALID_REQUEST | 401 (OpenAPI / access cookie) | 404 NOT_FOUND | 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR (ESI_INDUSTRY_UNAVAILABLE).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "200 \u2014 BlueprintV1[]",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}/blueprints",
            "description": "List of BlueprintV1 for the pilot. Requires ESI to answer for that character (auth cookie may be needed depending on ESI client config)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('body is BlueprintV1 array', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  if (body.length > 0) {",
                  "    pm.expect(body[0].jsonClass).to.eql('BlueprintV1');",
                  "    pm.expect(body[0]).to.have.property('blueprintId');",
                  "    pm.expect(body[0]).to.have.property('blueprintTypeId');",
                  "  }",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "400 \u2014 INVALID_REQUEST (pilotId not integer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{invalidPilotId}}/blueprints",
            "description": "ExceptionCatalog.INVALID_PILOT_ID \u2192 HTTP 400, code INVALID_REQUEST."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('NeocomError INVALID_REQUEST on pilotId', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].code).to.eql('INVALID_REQUEST');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].description).to.eql('pilotId must be an integer.');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].field).to.eql('pilotId');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].container).to.eql('path');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors[0].value).to.eql(pm.variables.get('invalidPilotId'));",
